-#### Early Splat Termination
-An optimization for volume splatting that skips processing of voxels when the accumulated opacity at the target screen pixels is already full, analogous to early ray termination in ray casting [S3]. It works by projecting two volumes: the density volume and an opacity volume [S3]. For each projected voxel, a 2D bounding box is computed around the pixels covering the splat [S3]. If all pixels inside the bounding box have full opacity (1.0 or near 1.0), the voxel processing is skipped [S3].
