-#### Hierarchical Splatting
-A progressive refinement algorithm for volume rendering using a pyramidal volume representation to achieve real-time interactive rendering [S6]. It constructs a pyramidal volume representation that stores average values and estimated error for each cell [S6]. It fits an octtree to the pyramid based on a user-supplied precision threshold [S6]. It draws the octtree using a set of splats (footprints), where each splat is scaled to match the size of the projection of the corresponding volume cell [S6]. It approximates the splats with RGBA Gouraud-shaded polygons for efficient rasterization on modern graphics workstations [S6].
